{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Eliphaz the Temanite</b> — from the family of Teman son of Eliphaz son of Esau. And it is likely that he lived long after the days of Moses, for [the name] would not be traced to Teman except after generations. And our Rabbis said that Moses wrote the book of Job. And it seems to me that it is a translated book; therefore it is difficult in interpretation, as is the way of every translated book." "<b>the Shuhite</b> — from the children of Keturah wife of Abraham: she bore Jokshan and Shuah." "<b>the Naamathite</b> — we do not know whether his lineage is traced to a region or to a family."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Reading והקרוב אלי ('and it seems to me'); some witnesses may read והקרוב שהיה קרוב ('and it is likely that he lived near'), reflecting the first occurrence of the phrase above."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:35.224763438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}